## 2. Covered Source

Covered Source means source code, documentation, configuration templates,
scripts, and related files that Tessallite intentionally publishes in the public
Tessallite Community repository and that do not carry a separate license notice.

Covered Source does not include:

- closed license manager implementations;
- gateway guard or admission-control modules;
- internal request-token issuer or verifier modules when shipped closed;
- model-service policy-enforcement modules or compiled model-service builds when
  shipped as closed artifacts;
- license issuer, signing, release, registry, website, or customer-provisioning
  systems;
- private release or signing automation;
- optional optimizer, acceleration planner, aggregate/pocket matcher, exactness
  validator, aggregate/pocket rewrite, and related private IP modules;
- compiled object code, container image layers, appliance images, VM images,
  hosted services, release bundles, or enterprise artifacts unless expressly
