- use the Covered Source to build or offer a competing commercial semantic
  layer, BI gateway, analytics platform, managed service, or substantially
  similar product;
- remove, obscure, or alter copyright, trademark, proprietary, or license
  notices;
- bypass, disable, or remove license checks, signed-license verification,
  gateway guards, internal request-token controls, or Community/Enterprise
  entitlement checks;
- reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, or attempt to extract source code
  from Closed Components except to the extent mandatory law permits it;
- publish, share, or distribute patches, forks, builds, images, or packages that
  include Closed Components or Tessallite proprietary material;
- use Tessallite names, logos, domains, marks, or brand assets except as allowed
